NNAAMMEE
     hhvv__vvssss__ddaaeemmoonn — Hyper-V Volume Shadow Copy Service Daemon

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     hhvv__vvssss__ddaaeemmoonn [--ddnn]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The hhvv__vvssss__ddaaeemmoonn daemon provides the ability to freeze and thaw the file
     system for FreeBSD guest partitions running on Hyper-V.

     Hyper-V allows administrators to backup or restore the FreeBSD guest par‐
     tition.  Administrators can use Windows Powershell scripts to backup or
     restore the FreeBSD VM.

     The hhvv__vvssss__ddaaeemmoonn accepts file system freeze and thaw requests from the
     hv_utils(4) driver and performs the actual file-system operation.

     The file system freeze and thaw functionality is useful when the Hyper-V
     host wants to do live backup of FreeBSD guest. Hyper-V host sends file
     system freezing request to hhvv__vvssss__ddaaeemmoonn which conducts the real opera‐
     tion. After successfully freezing file system, Hyper-V host takes a snap‐
     shot of the VM. In the future, Hyper-V host can restore the FreeBSD VM
     through that snapshot.

     The options are as follows:

     --dd      Run as regular process instead of a daemon for debugging purpose.

     --nn      Generate debugging output.

